    <string name="box64">Box64</string>
    <string name="box64_env_var_help__dynarec_bigblock">"Dynarec building BigBlock&lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>0&lt;/b> : Don't try to build block as big as possible&lt;br /> &lt;b>1&lt;/b> : Build Dynarec block as big as possible&lt;br /> &lt;b>2&lt;/b> : Build Dynarec block bigger (continue when block overlaps, but only for blocks in elf memory)&lt;br /> &lt;b>3&lt;/b> : Build Dynarec block bigger (continue when block overlaps, for all types of memory)"</string>
    <string name="box64_env_var_help__dynarec_callret">Optimization of CALL/RET opcodes</string>
    <string name="box64_env_var_help__dynarec_fastnan">Generation of -NAN like on x86</string>
    <string name="box64_env_var_help__dynarec_fastround">"Generation of precise x86 rounding&lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>0&lt;/b> : Generate float/double -> int rounding like on x86&lt;br /> &lt;b>1&lt;/b> : Don't do anything special with edge case Rounding, to go as fast as possible (no INF/NAN/Overflow -> MIN_INT conversion)&lt;br /> &lt;b>2&lt;/b> : Everything from 1 plus also fast round of double -> float (not taking into account current rounding mode)"</string>
    <string name="box64_env_var_help__dynarec_forward">Defines the max allowed forward value when building Block</string>
    <string name="box64_env_var_help__dynarec_nativeflags">The generated code will use native flags, if possible</string>
    <string name="box64_env_var_help__dynarec_safeflags">Handling of flags on CALL/RET opcodes&lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>0&lt;/b> : Treats CALL/RET as if it never needed flags (faster, unstable)&lt;br /> &lt;b>1&lt;/b> : Most RET will need flags, most CALLS will not&lt;br /> &lt;b>2&lt;/b> : All CALL/RET will need flags (slower)</string>
    <string name="box64_env_var_help__dynarec_strongmem">"Simulation of Strong Memory model&lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>0&lt;/b> : Don't try anything special&lt;br /> &lt;b>1&lt;/b> : Enable some Memory Barrier when writing to memory (on some MOV opcode)&lt;br /> &lt;b>2&lt;/b> : All 1 plus a Memory Barrier on every write to memory using MOV&lt;br /> &lt;b>3&lt;/b> : All 2 plus Memory Barrier when reading from memory and on some SSE/SSE2 opcodes"</string>
    <string name="box64_env_var_help__dynarec_wait">Defines whether or not Dynarec will wait for the FillBlock to be ready</string>
    <string name="box64_env_var_help__dynarec_weakbarrier">Tweak the memory barriers to reduce the performance impact by strongmem&lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>0&lt;/b> : Use regular safe barrier&lt;br /> &lt;b>1&lt;/b> : Use weak barriers to have more performance boost&lt;br /> &lt;b>2&lt;/b> : All in 1, plus disabled the last write barriers</string>
    <string name="box64_env_var_help__dynarec_x87double">Use of Float/Double for x87 emulation</string>
